Revision history for skills

{{$NEXT}}
  - New perl skill perl-par-binary-release: shipping a standalone PAR::Packer
    binary in a dist's GitHub release, from the release-binaries workflow to
    the build, verify, runtime-lib and smoke scripts.
  - Shared house rules: engineering-discipline, getty-agent-delegation,
    getty-publish-gate, getty-cpan-release and karr-coordination under
    rules/, installed through the bundles getty-house and getty-cpan-dist.
    getty-agent-team installs the bundle and keeps the project rules file to
    what is true in that repo.
  - New group game-development: ai-playable-games for the seat interface
    that lets bots and LLM agents play a game, simulation-balancing for
    balancing through bot leagues and mechanic ablation, game-balance-math
    for economy flows, cost curves and payoff matrices.
  - New group ai-engineering: ai-web-scraping for scraping, crawling and
    LLM-assisted extraction with field states and evidence-backed records;
    rocm-engineering for AMD GPU workloads on ROCm, from support matrices
    and installation to HIP, CUDA porting, AI frameworks and multi-GPU;
    vllm-operator lives there now instead of
    system-and-network-administration.
  - getty-perl-distribution and getty-agent-team: the agent and CI files ship
    with the release.

0.5.0     2026-10-22 22:38:58Z
  - New skills in system-and-network-administration: mikrotik-routeros,
    cisco-ios-router, cisco-small-business-switch and network-device-ssh-cli
    for routers and switches, proxmox-ve for Proxmox VE and Backup Server,
    samba-active-directory for Samba AD domains and file servers.
  - smart-home-devices: every vendor reference maps the manufacturer's whole
    range by line and generation (radio, HA route, caveat) and how to place a
    device from its label or model ID; Hue, Shelly, THIRDREALITY, Tuya,
    SONOFF, Zengge, BLE thermometers, Aqara/Xiaomi, OSRAM/LEDVANCE, Govee and
    Paulmann, with their sources.

0.4.0     2026-10-22 21:41:08Z
  - New group `compliance-and-governance`: EU compliance engineering for AI
    platforms with German overlays, entry point eu-platform-compliance and
    specialists for privacy, data governance, tracking and marketing, the AI
    Act, data and IP, consumer commerce, business contracts, billing and tax,
    accessibility, content safety, cybersecurity, agent assurance and
    regulatory watch, with its group image.
  - New skill storage-engineering in system-and-network-administration.
  - New group `smart-home`: Home Assistant (operator, automations, HACS),
    fritzbox-operator, smart-home-architecture, smart-home-devices,
    smart-home-radio, smart-home-esphome-mqtt and smart-home-video-media,
    with its group image.
  - Every skill description names only when to load the skill ("Use when …"):
    rewritten for electron-desktop-engineering, react-ecosystem-engineering,
    gearman, hetzner-operator, rex, ssl-tls-pki, kubernetes-cilium-concepts
    and all storytold-craft skills, with their MANIFEST.json hashes updated.

0.3.0     2026-10-20 23:04:10Z
  - New skill gearman in system-and-network-administration.
  - New group `javascript` with electron-desktop-engineering and
    react-ecosystem-engineering, with its group image.
  - getty-agent-team: covers skilletor shipping agents and rules (bundles for
    an agent plus its briefed skills), the settings.json entry skilletor
    writes itself, and the Codex agent form.
  - model-routing: Opus 5.5 is the strong default and beats Fable 5.1 in
    practice (docs and published benchmarks agree) at 40% of the cost; Fable
    stays as an exception tier, escalated to only after Opus at higher effort
    fails. Ladder updated to Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 5.5 (all 1M context).
    claude-headless follows.
  - getty-perl-core, getty-perl-moo and getty-perl-moose are smaller and
    match the code they describe: multi-line lists end with a trailing
    comma; `with` comes after the `use` lines and before `has`; Moo cleans
    with namespace::clean, Moose with namespace::autoclean; Moose has no
    `is => 'lazy'`. DBIC rules moved to getty-perl-core's references/dbic.md.
  - getty-perl-typing is smaller; Moose uses Types::Standard in new code,
    a dist already on string types (isa => 'Str') keeps them, parameter
    validation is Params::ValidationCompiler.
  - getty-perl-distribution: the author rule is fixed and the templates
    match real dists (0.001, aligned dist.ini, no stale pins).
  - getty-perl-sugar loads only when designing a new DSL; its authoring
    artifacts moved to perl/.dev/ and are no longer installed.

0.2.0     2026-10-13 05:16:08Z
  - New group storytold-craft: sixteen skills for operating the Storytold
    Craft editors as an agent, one per application plus an overview.
  - New skill getty-perl-sugar: declarative Perl DSL sugar on
    Moose::Exporter, with a metadata registry and one shared runner.
  - New groups codex, databases, hermes-agent and social-media.
  - New skills skill-mining, claude-cross-session,
    claude-code-plugin-engineering, getty-perl-typing, perl-alien,
    perl-mojo, perl-xs, docker-engine-api, hetzner-operator, ssl-tls-pki
    and vllm-operator.
  - docker, docker-registry, docker-engine-api and rex are routers over a
    reference tree; getty-rex is named rex.
  - getty-create-software lives in the development group.
  - getty-perl-kubernetes-classes, getty-perl-release-author-getty and
    perl-www-crawl4ai live in the repos that own their subject.
  - Skills are installed with skilletor; bin/check-listings holds the
    READMEs and both plugin manifests against the directories.
  - getty-git-commit-style prescribes one Changes file in the CPAN format
    for every repo.
  - Skill descriptions state when to load the skill, not what it contains.

0.1.0     2026-08-19 06:19:36Z
  - Initial library: authoring, claude, development, git, perl and
    system-and-network-administration, shipped as a plugin for Claude Code
    and for Codex.
